+"""Apply the v7.0.104 update to a v7.0.103 installation.
+
+Field case (job ``20261022-143856-7-small-daily-habits-tha-9729``, 2026-10-27 10:07 IST): the Queue panel said
+
+    Job needs recovery at shot_018 · 17/45 accepted shots are saved.
+    Flow video request is saved at …/flow/shots/shot_014/take_01.mp4.flow-request.json …
+    Cause: FlowRequestPending: Existing request still has no single identifiable asset …
+
+Two different shots in one notice. shot_014 had been downloaded and QC-accepted long before; the saved pause
+snapshot was simply never rewritten, so the panel described a request that no longer existed. In the same run a
+browser tab showed ``https://flow.google.com/404?reason=project`` ("Project not found") for a stored project URL,
+and the run reported it as the generic "composer was not found".
+
+v7.0.104:
+
+- ``engine/pause_freshness.py`` rewrites a saved pause before it is shown: if the reason quotes a journal that is
+  no longer unresolved, or the production has moved past the saved shot, the notice says it was superseded, names
+  the requests that *are* still open and where Resume continues; the old text is kept, not hidden;
+- ``FlowProjectMissing`` is raised when a stored project URL answers "Project not found" (three short retries
+  first, because a project created seconds ago can 404 while Flow provisions it);
+- the job pauses with ``flow_project_missing`` and a message that names the dead URL, the local file that stores
+  it, and the exact ``flow-projects --clear-video`` / ``--set-stills`` repair - no silent fallback;
+- the Job panel and ``python3 cli.py v3 status <job>`` show that message and both bindings.
+
+Nothing is generated, rendered or charged by this update itself.
+
+Usage (run from the existing installation folder, after extracting the 7.0.104 zip beside it):
+
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.104/tools/update_v7103_to_v7104.py .            # dry run: shows the plan
+    python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.104/tools/update_v7103_to_v7104.py . --apply    # installs the code
+
+Only code and documentation are replaced. Outputs, saved jobs, Flow journals, browser profiles and
+Clip Studio folders are never copied, moved or deleted. Stop the dashboard before --apply.
+"""
+
+
+import argparse
+import datetime
+import fcntl
+import hashlib
+import json
+import os
+import shutil
+import tempfile
+from pathlib import Path
+
+CHANGES = ['FLOW_PROJECT_404_V7_0_104.md', 'VERSION', 'app.py', 'cli.py', 'engine/factory.py',
+           'engine/job_activity.py', 'engine/pause_freshness.py', 'engine/providers/flow_browser.py',
+           'tests/test_v7104_stale_pause_and_404.py', 'tools/update_v7103_to_v7104.py']
+# Files as they exist in 7.0.103: the only hashes this updater will replace.
+# A hash outside this list means local edits; the file is preserved and nothing is applied.
+ALLOWED = {
+    'VERSION': ['7ac5202f82dbff715a969cea1929f6a1701481ce3267e5fbd4eef5bf2a8abccd'],
+    'app.py': ['80a69a657aad67ab8ed6d9bf2fecb4f9318b984cbd4164c88229e2962682081b'],
+    'cli.py': ['67488a09529c2885c26bacea319b232c8595b71a8ae2c88bd092323dc152b041'],
